author: codex-searxng-agent
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "The actual searxng CLI reports current, stale, or unavailable source freshness by comparing the configured service version/commit with official searxng/searxng master without treating network failures as stale; TOON 4.1.0 is the default lossless format and all strict decode/validation/schema contracts pass; Global settings/setup/cache remain under ~/.searxng-cli, governed URL remains http://192.168.1.183:38522, and zero-limit cache persistence is unchanged; Repo-local pm-cli and pm-changelog are current and all project packages activate without quarantine; 100/100/100/100 coverage, 100 percent module docstrings, lint, duplication, security, PM, installed package, live LAN, PR bot, merge, and release gates pass"
definition_of_ready: "All 56 PM items and 650 verified histories, all statuses, duplicate searches, 152-edge graph analytics, current official SearXNG and TOON sources, live instance metadata, npm registry, source/tests/docs, and GitHub state were inspected; no active or duplicate item covers this delta."
goal: Continuously current agent-native SearXNG CLI
objective: Live source freshness and TOON 4.1 correctness
value: Agents can prove that searches use the governed service and whether that service matches current upstream
impact: Turns documentation freshness from a manual assertion into a machine-readable runtime contract while preserving full feature parity
outcome: A release-ready CLI with self-verifying upstream compatibility and current lossless output/tooling
why_now: TOON 4.1.0 and PM 2026.7.27 shipped after the previous release; the older project PM package set is now quarantined by the current host.
reviewer: github-bots
risk: high
confidence: 94
sprint: 2026-07-current-compatibility
release: 2026.7.28
