comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T21:16:45.583Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Pre-mutation census: 56 closed items, zero active items, 650 history entries, 152 relationship edges, zero graph or duplicate findings. Official docs are build b060c780d and the governed service reports the identical 2026.7.26+b060c780d version. TOON 4.1.0 and PM/pm-changelog 2026.7.27 are confirmed registry latest."
  "2026-07-27T21:31:19.288Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Release note: direct release:dry-run correctly rejected the still-unreleased 2026.7.26 package version because today's next version is 2026.7.27. The clean-tree release:pipeline:dry-run will perform its governed temporary version/changelog generation after the implementation commit; do not hand-edit package version or generated CHANGELOG.md."
  "2026-07-27T21:36:27.680Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Acceptance checkpoint: PM test ran all five non-duplicated commands with zero failures or skipped gates. The installed package resolved its own searxng binary from an isolated prefix and confirmed the configured service is current at b060c780d, default TOON 4.1 output, ~/.searxng-cli state, and unlimited cache. Release pipeline dry-run temporarily produced v2026.7.27, passed version/tag/changelog/history/build/coverage/package gates, and restored a clean tree."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T21:16:45.583Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Do not persist raw live payloads, credentials, private topology beyond the governed service URL, or transient signed data in PM/GitHub. Source freshness must distinguish unavailable from stale."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T21:16:45.583Z",codex-searxng-agent,Current compatibility is strongest when the installed CLI emits provenance for both the live service commit and the official upstream head instead of relying on a checked-at documentation sentence.
